      "note": "Common collocations: 发行债券 (issue bonds), 购买债券 (buy bonds), 债券市场 (bond market), 债券价格 / 债券收益率 (bond price / yield). 国债 = government bond.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "zh": "政府今年计划发行更多债券。",
          "py": "Zhèngfǔ jīnnián jìhuà fāxíng gèng duō zhàiquàn.",
          "en": "The government plans to issue more bonds this year."
        },
        {
          "zh": "最近债券价格上涨，收益率下降了。",
          "py": "Zuìjìn zhàiquàn jiàgé shàngzhǎng, shōuyìlǜ xiàjiàng le.",
          "en": "Bond prices have risen recently, and yields have fallen."
        },
        {
          "zh": "我爸爸觉得买债券比买股票更安全。",
          "py": "Wǒ bàba juéde mǎi zhàiquàn bǐ mǎi gǔpiào gèng ānquán.",
          "en": "My dad thinks buying bonds is safer than buying stocks."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "hanzi": "流动性",
      "pinyin": "liúdòngxìng",
      "pos": "noun",
      "en": "liquidity",
      "note": "常见搭配：流动性支持 (liquidity support)、流动性风险 (liquidity risk)、提供流动性 (provide liquidity)、流动性紧张 (tight liquidity).",
      "examples": [
        {
          "zh": "央行推出新工具，给市场提供流动性。",
          "py": "Yāngháng tuīchū xīn gōngjù, gěi shìchǎng tígōng liúdòngxìng.",
          "en": "The central bank launched a new tool to provide liquidity to the market."
        },
        {
          "zh": "现金的流动性最好，房子的流动性比较差。",
          "py": "Xiànjīn de liúdòngxìng zuì hǎo, fángzi de liúdòngxìng bǐjiào chà.",
          "en": "Cash is the most liquid; a house is fairly illiquid."
        },
        {
          "zh": "我们每天都要检查公司账户的流动性够不够。",
          "py": "Wǒmen měi tiān dōu yào jiǎnchá gōngsī zhànghù de liúdòngxìng gòu bu gòu.",
          "en": "Every day we check whether the company's accounts have enough liquidity."
        }
      ]
    }
